Name:           tcode
Version:        @VERSION@
Release:        1%{?dist}
Summary:        lightweight text editor written in Lua
License:        MIT
BuildArch:      x86_64
Requires:       SDL3, luajit OR lua
Suggests:       xdg-utils

%description
T Code is a lightweight text editor written mostly in Lua, on top of a
minimalistic C core using the SDL3 graphics library.

%prep
%autosetup -p1

%build
meson setup --buildtype=release --prefix=/usr/local --wrap-mode=forcefallback build
meson compile -C build

%install
DESTDIR=%{buildroot} meson install -C build --skip-subprojects=freetype2,lua,pcre2

%files
/usr/local/bin/tcode
/usr/local/share/tcode/
/usr/local/share/doc/tcode/
/usr/local/share/icons/hicolor/scalable/apps/tcode.svg
/usr/local/share/applications/dev.thinakaran.tcode.desktop
/usr/local/share/metainfo/dev.thinakaran.tcode.metainfo.xml
/usr/local/share/man/man1/tcode.1.gz

%changelog
* Sat Nov 07 2026 Thinakaran Manokaran <https://thinakaran.dev/> @VERSION@-1
- Initial RPM packaging.
